  "note": "Independent re-judgment against RFC 4659 Section 3.2.1.1 ('The link-local address shall be included in the Next Hop field if and only if the advertising BGP speaker shares a common subnet with the peer the route is being advertised to [BGP-IPv6].') after export-chain next-hop unification (cabc8c511e / c2d7117d05). Re-read all tagged tests (including migrated export-policy fixtures in rfc4659_vpn_link_local_loopback_test.go, rfc4659_vpn_link_local_test.go, and rfc4659_vpn_next_hop_rewrite_test.go) and all four producer boundaries (applyLinkLocal, normalizeOrdinaryNextHop, applyEgressNextHopScope, linkScope.linkLocalNextHop). Export-chain unification preserved exact 48-octet common-subnet and 24-octet off-subnet assertions when session > link-local is explicitly configured. However, the default-path defect remains unchanged: applyLinkLocal still permits an absent link-local leaf and linkScope.linkLocalNextHop (case nextHopRouterSpeaker) still returns an empty netip.Addr{} whenever configured LinkLocal is unset, omitting the required link-local address on a common subnet under default configuration, and no tagged test exercises interface-derived speaker link-local selection. Retain verdict: weak.",
